  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Project Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the modular `TermLink` monorepo packages. I\'m carefully reviewing the dependency DAG. Right now, I\'m working with the core package which contains types, configuration schema validation, safe filename/path guards, a dangerous command detector, a structured logger, error classes, and constants. My aim is to build cleanly without circular dependencies.\n\n\n**Clarifying Core Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the package dependencies, and how to structure everything for maximum flexibility. The `packages/core` module looks good, so I\'m focusing on the `permissions`, `protocol`, and `identity` modules. Right now, `packages/permissions` only needs `packages/core`. The `protocol` module also needs the `core` one, and I\'ve started on `identity`, which will use Node\'s `crypto` module.\n\n\n**Refining Identity Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `packages/identity` module. I\'m focusing on features such as 256-bit fingerprints, secure local identity persistence, and the creation of trusted and revoked device stores. I\'m also working on device renaming and identity reset functionalities. A public key export mechanism is also planned to be implemented, while staying dependent on `packages/core`.\n\n\n\n**Expanding Network Features**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design of networking components. The chunk distribution coordinator will implement integrity verification and backpressure. It will also have pause/resume/cancel and conflict-safe destination naming. I\'m also planning for local transfer history and will reject symlinks. This depends on `packages/core` and `packages/protocol`.\n\n\n**Developing Network Protocols**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the network components. I\'ve been working on the `P2PTransport` which is a direct TCP peer-to-peer socket, including an Ed25519 handshake and AES-256-GCM framing. I\'m also implementing automatic detection of network types, with an encrypted WebSocket relay fallback if direct connection fails. I\'m also aiming for (N-1)/2 connection tracking and selective/hybrid topology with 9-20 peers. This depends on several other packages.\n\n\n**Designing Developer SDK**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the public developer SDK, specifically the `TermLink` class, `RoomSession`, and the typed event emitter for seamless interaction. I\'m also thinking through how these features work across real Node.js processes. Next I will be working on signaling server features.\n\n\n\n"
    message_id: "r_T_avPRMpuF28oP3LOz4Qk"
