  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Drafting Documentation Outlines**\n\nI\'m now outlining key documents: `README.md`, an architectural overview (`docs/architecture.md`), networking/VM details (`docs/networking-and-vms.md`), SDK/CLI instructions (`docs/sdk-and-cli.md`), and troubleshooting guidance (`docs/troubleshooting.md`). These will cover VMware (scenarios A-E), VirtualBox, setup across Windows/Linux/macOS, self-hosting signaling, and TURN server considerations.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "1v3_avnXBv-9vdIPjt2zMA"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14360532097460565039"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# TermLink\\n\\n**Connect terminals. Share files. Collaborate directly.**\\n\\nTermLink is a cross-platform, peer-to-peer terminal collaboration platform for Windows, Linux, macOS, physical machines, cloud VMs, VMware, VirtualBox, and WSL2.\\n\\nOpen a terminal, get a **2-digit room code (`00`\342\200\223`99`)** and invite link, approve joining peers by cryptographic fingerprint, chat in real time, transfer files with chunked SHA-256 integrity verification, propose commands safely, and optionally share host terminal sessions with per-peer permissions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Core Capabilities\\n\\n- **2-Digit Quick Connect (`00`\342\200\223`99`)**: Instant discovery codes with host approval by default, sliding-window rate limiting, short TTL, code rotation, and safe multi-room collision disambiguation.\\n- **Secure Invitation Links**: Configurable `/join/<code>` and cryptographically random `/invite/<token>` links with role scoping, expiration, one-time use, and instant revocation.\\n- **End-to-End Encrypted Group Rooms**: Full mesh topology for 2\342\200\2238 peers (`N \303\227 (N - 1) / 2`) and selective hybrid topology for 9\342\200\22320 peers. Uses Ed25519 signing, X25519 key exchange, and AES-256-GCM encryption.\\n- **Real P2P Transport + Honest Relay Fallback**: Direct TCP P2P (CLI/SDK) and WebRTC DataChannels (Web Companion) with RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing and opaque E2EE relay fallback. Accurately displays `Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, or `Disconnected`.\\n- **Chunked Streaming File Transfer**: Streaming I/O with 64 KiB chunks, per-chunk and full-file SHA-256 verification, backpressure, pause/resume/cancel, explicit recipient approval, path traversal protection, and conflict-free destination naming.\\n- **Opt-In Remote Terminal Sharing**: Disabled by default. Requires explicit host activation, per-peer `read-only` or `interactive` grants, session locking, instant revocation, and local audit logs.\\n- **Safe Command Proposals**: Send commands for peer review (`Accept` / `Edit` / `Reject`) with automatic high-risk command warnings (`rm -rf`, `curl | sh`, `mkfs`, `dd`). Never auto-executed.\\n- **Role-Based Permissions**: `Owner`, `Admin`, `Collaborator`, `Viewer`, and `Guest`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### 1. Run Signaling Server + Web Companion (Local Dev)\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install\\nnpm run dev\\n```\\n\\nOpen `http://localhost:3000` (WebSocket signaling runs at `ws://localhost:3000/ws`).\\n\\n### 2. Connect via CLI\\n\\n**Computer A (Host):**\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run cli -- create --name \\\"DEV TEAM\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Computer B (Join via 2-digit code):**\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run cli -- 47\\n```\\n\\n**Or via invite link:**\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run cli -- join http://localhost:3000/invite/<TOKEN>\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Global npm Installation (when published)\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install -g termlink\\ntermlink\\n```\\n\\nOr run without installing globally:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpx termlink\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLI Command Reference\\n\\n```bash\\ntermlink                           # Interactive menu\\ntermlink 47                        # Quick-join room 47\\ntermlink create                    # Create room & display 2-digit code\\ntermlink host                      # Alias for create\\ntermlink join 47                   # Join by 2-digit code\\ntermlink join <URL>                # Join by /join/NN or /invite/TOKEN link\\ntermlink room lookup 47            # Inspect public candidates for code 47\\ntermlink send <file> --code 47 --group\\ntermlink send <file> --code 47 --to RAHUL-LAPTOP\\ntermlink diagnostics [--detailed] [--json]\\ntermlink config                    # Print local config\\ntermlink config set <key> <value>  # Update config key\\ntermlink config reset              # Restore defaults\\ntermlink devices                   # Show local identity & trusted devices\\ntermlink trust revoke <id>         # Revoke device trust\\ntermlink status                    # Check local node & signaling status\\ntermlink version                   # Print TermLink version\\n```\\n\\nInside an active room session:\\n\\n```text\\n/members \302\267 /status \302\267 /msg <peer> <text> \302\267 /send <file> \302\267 /approve <reqId>\\n/reject <reqId> \302\267 /accept-file <id> \302\267 /propose <peer> <cmd> \302\267 /invite\\n/rotate \302\267 /share-term \302\267 /stop-term \302\267 /clear \302\267 /help \302\267 /leave\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Repository Architecture\\n\\n```text\\ntermlink/\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 apps/\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 cli/                 # Cross-platform TermLink CLI & executable bin\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 signaling-server/    # Lightweight WebSocket signaling & opaque E2EE relay\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 packages/\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 core/                # Shared types, config validator, path/command security\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 identity/            # Ed25519 + X25519 + AES-256-GCM & local trust store\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 protocol/            # Wire schemas, join link parser, peer-assist manifest\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 permissions/         # RBAC permission engine (Owner -> Guest)\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 room-engine/         # 2-digit codes, collisions, invites, rate limits\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 file-transfer/       # Streaming chunked sender/receiver + SHA-256\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 terminal-session/    # Cross-platform shell adapter, RBAC & audit log\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 networking/          # Topology manager, RFC 5389 STUN, Direct TCP E2EE\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 diagnostics/         # Signaling, STUN, socket & interface diagnostics\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 sdk/                 # Public TypeScript Developer SDK\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/                     # Live Web Companion (WebRTC + WebSocket + UI)\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                # Unified Express + WebSocket + Vite server\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/                   # Unit, multi-peer integration, and security suites\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docs/                    # Architecture, VMware/VM, SDK, troubleshooting docs\\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 .github/workflows/       # Cross-platform CI (Windows/Ubuntu/macOS) & Release\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- [Architecture & Protocol](docs/architecture.md)\\n- [Networking, Self-Hosting, TURN & VMware/VirtualBox Guide](docs/networking-and-vms.md)\\n- [Developer SDK & npm Publishing Guide](docs/sdk-and-cli.md)\\n- [Troubleshooting & Platform Notes](docs/troubleshooting.md)\\n- [Security & Threat Model](SECURITY.md)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verification & Testing\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run lint         # TypeScript type-checking\\nnpm test             # Unit + multi-peer integration + security tests\\nnpm run build        # Production web companion bundle\\nnpm run pack:check   # Validate npm package tarball (npm pack --dry-run)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Roadmap\\n\\n- Peer-assisted chunk redistribution UI & automated swarm scheduling (protocol module included in `packages/protocol`)\\n- Optional native `node-pty` adapter plugin for full-screen curses/vim terminal emulation\\n- Optional native WebRTC DataChannel transport provider for CLI-to-Browser direct UDP traversal\\n- Persistent team workspaces, session recordings, and desktop/mobile companion apps\\n\\n## License\\n\\nMIT \342\200\224 see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write comprehensive README.md covering setup, CLI, architecture, testing, and roadmap\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/README.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing README.md\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write project README\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\346\003\n\343\003\001i\024}\023\307\331\034\257\375\n\f\232\367\373I\327#\1776\036\274\036\341j\355\364nA\025\003\372\317\\\023E\027b\376\263:\262\244\277\365T\233B\271\373\261\032\333p\232\343D\263\n\356\231\273j\022\367\354\354H\234\321\313\305\210\240\315\001*\265X\032`\265&\201I\237j&\346\t\367\344S\037\263\226aYg\300\2528LU\324\fO\223\221\325\241\354\332\210\341\305\371\204\332\315`\261\361F)\027E\205&\323\a\216\031Mq:Y7\223\263#7\256\222\030i\233/\262Y\302S\3516N#\346_\233\031\262\311\247`9f\325m\337\024\242|\210\324\345S\360\001}}\'K\261\341D\206\311R\216\303\232\215u\373~\"\337\023A\244\363S\233\256\034\322\003\305Q\217\257*\324|K20\257\255*\267\314B\230\262\277\225\004[SI\352\377;\031\321\\\203\264,\3125\326\326JE\266/7\353f\034;}\255\213\251\231`f\233{\263\233\370D\247\322\304\364\350\220\025\3607\003\232\234\324h\035\220\204\336[_\234\212-={X\240ml\324\332\020frH\214\fK\206 \333[\373\211\326I\020\251K\265J\223in0\027\274\352s\275\036\246r\326\232\210\016\177k\250\363\275s\r\220\370\215\021g\3601klf?\220s\260w\377\224\305\271\354\347W\360k\354G\001\037}\311e\204@\312>\211+\273\315\025\265\365\256\332\244\311\356\t?\217\037\231%Tu\016\316\232\374*\223\v\v\005\255\324\371E\307\035\2357\ru\361\333\217\200\265i\306\0029k\264\2738\312\246\002Z\344\255\b>\237\310\363q\337\242\376\257\371\023\317\315\233+\316\a[\344=\251\253\353\023\247k\034\334\262\341~\023&\266\355\253\324\322\206\212!\320\272%\306\253\310\210\361"
