    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14360532097460567074"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# TermLink Architecture & Protocol\\n\\n## Layered Modular Design\\n\\nTermLink separates networking, protocol validation, security policy, terminal execution, and user interfaces into isolated workspace packages without circular dependencies:\\n\\n1. `@termlink/core`: Shared TypeScript contracts, configuration validation, filename/path-traversal protection, command risk analysis, and structured logging.\\n2. `@termlink/permissions`: Pure RBAC engine governing `owner`, `admin`, `collaborator`, `viewer`, and `guest` privileges plus terminal interactive grants.\\n3. `@termlink/protocol`: Wire schemas, strict incoming frame validation (`256 KiB` control frame ceiling), join target parser (`47`, `/join/47`, `/invite/<token>`, `termlink://...`), and the future-ready `PeerAssistedManifest` module.\\n4. `@termlink/identity`: Local cryptographic keypair management (Ed25519 signatures + X25519 Diffie-Hellman + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM), SHA-256 fingerprint formatting, and `0o600` local trust store.\\n5. `@termlink/room-engine`: Ephemeral 2-digit code allocator (`00`\342\200\223`99`), collision resolution, scrypt password hashing, cryptographic invitation tokens (TTL, one-time, revocation), sliding-window anti-enumeration rate limiter, and reconnection tokens.\\n6. `@termlink/networking`: `TopologyManager` (`N*(N-1)/2` full mesh up to 8 peers, hybrid selective links for 9\342\200\22320 peers), real RFC 5389 UDP STUN client (`node:dgram`), and `DirectP2PTransport` with transparent E2EE relay fallback.\\n7. `@termlink/file-transfer`: Streaming `fs.createReadStream` / `fs.createWriteStream` chunked transfer protocol (64 KiB chunks, per-chunk SHA-256, full-file SHA-256, backpressure ACKs, `.part` staging, conflict-free destination naming).\\n8. `@termlink/terminal-session`: Cross-platform shell abstraction (`powershell.exe` on Windows, `$SHELL`/`bash`/`zsh`/`sh` on Unix), disabled by default, per-peer access matrix, session lock, and audit logging.\\n9. `@termlink/diagnostics`: Real signaling RTT, UDP STUN binding test, TCP listener capability test, and privacy-respecting network interface inspection.\\n10. `@termlink/sdk`: Public event-driven developer API (`TermLink` + `RoomSession`).\\n\\n## Transport & Encryption Flow\\n\\n1. Peers connect to the lightweight signaling server (`ws://` or `wss://`) and send `hello` containing **only their public keys and fingerprint**.\\n2. Room discovery uses 2-digit codes or secure invite tokens. Host approval verifies peer fingerprints before issuing peer endpoints.\\n3. Peers exchange endpoints (Direct TCP for CLI/SDK, WebRTC SDP/ICE for browser peers) and establish direct peer-to-peer links whenever NAT/firewalls permit.\\n4. Every application message (chat, file offers/chunks, command proposals, terminal streams) is encrypted pairwise with AES-256-GCM and signed before transmission.\\n5. If direct connection fails, envelopes automatically fall back to the signaling server\'s opaque relay handler\342\200\224and the UI explicitly labels the peer as `Relayed`.\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write docs/architecture.md detailing package DAG, protocol, and encryption flow\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/docs/architecture.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing architecture documentation\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write architecture docs\"}"
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14360532097460565013"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# Networking, Self-Hosting, TURN & Virtual Machines (VMware / VirtualBox / WSL2)\\n\\n## Self-Hosting the Signaling Server\\n\\nRun the standalone lightweight signaling server on any Linux/Windows/macOS host or VPS:\\n\\n```bash\\nPORT=8787 TERMLINK_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://termlink.yourdomain.com npm run signaling\\n```\\n\\nPoint CLI peers to your server:\\n\\n```bash\\ntermlink config set signalingServer wss://termlink.yourdomain.com/ws\\ntermlink config set publicBaseUrl https://termlink.yourdomain.com\\n```\\n\\nAlways terminate TLS (`wss://` and `https://`) via Caddy, Nginx, or a cloud load balancer in production. Never hardcode a domain you do not own.\\n\\n## Configuring STUN & TURN Relay Servers\\n\\nFor strict corporate NAT or symmetric firewalls, configure STUN and TURN servers in `~/.termlink/config.json`:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"stunServers\\\": [\\n    \\\"stun:stun.l.google.com:19302\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"turnServers\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"urls\\\": \\\"turn:turn.yourdomain.com:3478\\\",\\n      \\\"username\\\": \\\"termlink\\\",\\n      \\\"credential\\\": \\\"SET_VIA_ENV_OR_LOCAL_SECRET\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\nWhen no external TURN server is configured and direct P2P cannot connect, TermLink falls back to end-to-end encrypted relay forwarding over the signaling WebSocket and accurately displays `Relayed`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## VMware, VirtualBox & WSL2 Scenarios\\n\\nTermLink runs natively inside the guest OS (Windows, Ubuntu, Kali, Debian, Fedora, Arch, macOS). No VMware-specific driver is required.\\n\\n### Scenario A: Windows Host + Ubuntu VMware Guest\\n- **Network Mode**: Bridged (recommended) or NAT.\\n- **Host (Windows PowerShell)**: `termlink create --name \\\"HOST-VM-LAB\\\"` -> displays 2-digit code (e.g., `47`).\\n- **Guest (Ubuntu Terminal)**: `termlink 47` -> host approves Ubuntu guest\'s fingerprint.\\n- **Expected Transport**: `Local network` on Bridged mode; `Local network` or `Relayed` on NAT depending on host firewall rules.\\n\\n### Scenario B: Windows Host + Kali VMware Guest + Ubuntu VM (3-Peer Group)\\n- All three machines configure the same `signalingServer` (either hosted on the Windows host LAN IP e.g. `ws://192.168.1.10:3000/ws`, or a shared HTTPS/WSS server).\\n- Host runs `termlink create`; Kali and Ubuntu guests both run `termlink <code>`.\\n- Full mesh establishes `3 \303\227 2 / 2 = 3` encrypted pairwise links.\\n\\n### Scenario C: Separate Physical Computers & VMs Across Different Networks\\n- Point all peers to a publicly reachable TLS signaling server (`wss://...`).\\n- TermLink probes UDP STUN for NAT traversal and falls back automatically to E2EE relay when symmetric NAT blocks direct packets.\\n\\n### Scenario D: Host-Only Networking (VMware VMnet1 / VirtualBox vboxnet0)\\n- **Limitation**: Host-only adapters have **no internet access** and cannot reach public STUN servers (`stun.l.google.com`).\\n- **How to run**: Start the signaling server on the host machine bound to `0.0.0.0:3000`, find the host\'s host-only IP (e.g., `192.168.56.1`), and run:\\n  ```bash\\n  termlink config set signalingServer ws://192.168.56.1:3000/ws\\n  ```\\n- Direct LAN P2P works cleanly between the host and all VMs on that host-only subnet.\\n\\n### Scenario E: NAT Networking Limitations\\n- VMware/VirtualBox NAT places the guest behind a second NAT layer (Double NAT).\\n- Outbound connections to the signaling server work immediately, while inbound direct connections to the guest may be blocked by the hypervisor NAT.\\n- **Verification**: Run `termlink diagnostics --detailed` inside the guest to inspect `Signaling`, `STUN`, `Direct P2P`, and `Relay` readiness.\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write docs/networking-and-vms.md covering self-hosting, TURN, and VMware/VirtualBox Scenarios A through E\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/docs/networking-and-vms.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing networking & VM documentation\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write networking and VMware guide\"}"
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14360532097460567048"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# Developer SDK & npm Publishing Guide\\n\\n## Using the TypeScript SDK\\n\\n```typescript\\nimport { TermLink } from \\\"termlink\\\";\\n\\nconst client = new TermLink({\\n  deviceName: \\\"AADI-PC\\\",\\n  signalingServer: \\\"ws://localhost:3000/ws\\\",\\n});\\n\\nawait client.initialize();\\n\\nconst room = await client.createRoom({\\n  roomName: \\\"DEV TEAM\\\",\\n  requireHostApproval: true,\\n});\\n\\nconsole.log(\\\"Room code:\\\", room.code);\\n\\nroom.on(\\\"joinRequest\\\", (req) => {\\n  console.log(`Incoming peer: ${req.identity.deviceName} (${req.identity.fingerprint})`);\\n  room.approveJoin(req.requestId, \\\"collaborator\\\");\\n});\\n\\nroom.on(\\\"peerJoined\\\", (peer) => {\\n  console.log(`${peer.identity.deviceName} connected`);\\n});\\n\\nroom.on(\\\"message\\\", (msg) => {\\n  console.log(`[${msg.senderName}] ${msg.text}`);\\n});\\n\\nawait room.sendMessage(\\\"Hello, everyone!\\\");\\n```\\n\\n### Public `RoomSession` Methods & Events\\n\\n- **Methods**: `approveJoin`, `rejectJoin`, `kickPeer`, `setPeerRole`, `transferOwnership`, `rotateCode`, `createInvite`, `revokeInvite`, `updateSettings`, `sendMessage`, `sendPrivateMessage`, `proposeCommand`, `sendFile`, `pauseFileTransfer`, `resumeFileTransfer`, `cancelFileTransfer`, `startTerminalSession`, `setTerminalPeerAccess`, `lockTerminalSession`, `stopTerminalSession`, `sendTerminalInput`, `leave`, `closeRoom`.\\n- **Events**: `joinRequest`, `peerJoined`, `peerLeft`, `roomUpdated`, `roomClosed`, `inviteCreated`, `inviteRevoked`, `message`, `privateMessage`, `messageDelivered`, `fileOffer`, `fileProgress`, `fileComplete`, `fileRejected`, `fileCancelled`, `commandProposal`, `commandDecision`, `terminalState`, `terminalOutput`, `connectionStateChanged`, `securityWarning`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## npm Packaging & Release Checklist\\n\\nBefore publishing to npm (never publish automatically without maintainer approval):\\n\\n1. Update `\\\"version\\\"` in `package.json` following SemVer.\\n2. Run full verification:\\n   ```bash\\n   npm run lint\\n   npm test\\n   npm run build\\n   npm pack --dry-run\\n   ```\\n3. Verify the tarball includes `apps/cli/bin/termlink.mjs`, `apps/cli/src`, `apps/signaling-server/src`, `packages/*/src`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`, and `SECURITY.md`, and excludes private keys, `.env`, or temporary files.\\n4. Create an annotated git tag (`git tag -a v1.0.0 -m \\\"Release v1.0.0\\\"`) and push to trigger the approval-gated `.github/workflows/release.yml` workflow.\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write docs/sdk-and-cli.md with SDK API documentation and npm release checklist\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/docs/sdk-and-cli.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing SDK and publishing docs\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write SDK and npm release guide\"}"
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14360532097460564987"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# Troubleshooting & Platform Setup\\n\\n## Quick Diagnostics Command\\n\\nAlways start by running:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run cli -- diagnostics --detailed\\n```\\n\\n## Common Issues\\n\\n### 1. Signaling Shows \\\"Disconnected\\\"\\n- Confirm the signaling server is running (`npm run dev` on port 3000, or `npm run signaling` on port 8787).\\n- Check your configured URL: `npm run cli -- config` -> verify `signalingServer`.\\n- On VMs, replace `localhost` with the host machine\'s LAN or Host-Only IP address.\\n\\n### 2. Connection Shows \\\"Relayed\\\" Instead of \\\"Direct P2P\\\"\\n- Direct P2P requires either a shared LAN/VPN or compatible NAT traversal.\\n- Windows Defender Firewall or `ufw` on Linux may block inbound ephemeral TCP/UDP sockets. Allow Node.js on Private networks if you want direct LAN sockets.\\n- Relayed traffic remains **end-to-end encrypted (AES-256-GCM)**; TermLink intentionally reports `Relayed` so you always know the real transport path.\\n\\n### 3. Multiple Rooms Share the Same 2-Digit Code\\n- Two-digit codes have 100 slots (`00`\342\200\223`99`). When two active public rooms share a code, TermLink displays all candidates with host device name, platform, and fingerprint prefix so you can select the exact room you intended.\\n- For private or high-traffic deployments, disable `publicQuickConnect` and share a secure `/invite/<TOKEN>` link.\\n\\n### 4. Windows / PowerShell / Command Prompt Notes\\n- TermLink automatically detects `powershell.exe` on Windows and never assumes `/bin/bash` exists.\\n- Classic `cmd.exe` without UTF-8 automatically receives ASCII box-drawing fallbacks (`+===+`) instead of broken Unicode characters.\\n\\n### 5. Linux / macOS Permissions\\n- Local identity secrets are stored in `~/.termlink/identity.secret.json` with mode `0600`.\\n- If you move or reset devices, run `termlink trust reset-identity` to generate a fresh Ed25519 + X25519 keypair.\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write docs/troubleshooting.md covering diagnostics, firewalls, code collisions, and Windows/Linux/macOS notes\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/docs/troubleshooting.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing troubleshooting guide\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write troubleshooting documentation\"}"
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 48
      nanos: 77001352
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "1v3_avnXBv-9vdIPjt2zMA"
  }
}
