  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Build **TermLink** (`termlink`), a production-oriented, cross-platform, peer-to-peer **terminal collaboration npm package** (`npm install -g termlink` / `npx termlink` / `termlink`) that runs directly in Windows, Linux, macOS, physical machine, cloud VM, VMware, VirtualBox, and WSL2 terminals.\n- **User Clarification (CRITICAL)**: In Turn 2, the user explicitly objected to having a React/Vite web dashboard (\"why you made website?? i told you to make npm package which will run in terminal of the computer\"). All web frontend files (`/src/`, `/index.html`, `/vite.config.ts`) were deleted and the project was converted into a pure Node.js npm CLI + Signaling Server + Developer SDK package compiled into `dist/`.\n- **Core Features Required**:\n  - 2-digit quick-connect room codes (`00`\342\200\223`99`) with collision resolution, TTL, rate limiting, and default host approval\n  - Secure invitation links (`/join/NN` and `/invite/TOKEN`) with expiration, one-time use, role scoping, and revocation\n  - Group rooms (2\342\200\2238 full mesh `N*(N-1)/2`, 9\342\200\22320 hybrid selective topology)\n  - Real P2P networking (Direct TCP with X25519 + Ed25519 + AES-256-GCM E2EE, RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing, opaque E2EE relay fallback with honest transport reporting: `Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, `Disconnected`)\n  - E2EE group & private chat with slash commands (`/msg`, `/members`, `/status`, `/clear`, `/help`, `/leave`)\n  - Real streaming chunked P2P file transfer (64 KiB chunks, per-chunk + full-file SHA-256 verification, backpressure, pause/resume/cancel, explicit recipient approval, path traversal/symlink guards, conflict-free non-overwriting destination paths, plus future-ready peer-assisted distribution protocol module)\n  - Opt-in host-controlled remote terminal sharing (disabled by default, cross-platform shell selection PowerShell/bash/zsh/sh, per-peer `read-only`/`interactive`/`disabled` permissions, locking, instant revocation, audit log)\n  - Safe command proposals (never auto-executed, dangerous-command risk detection)\n  - Local cryptographic identity & trust store (`0o600`), RBAC (`owner`, `admin`, `collaborator`, `viewer`, `guest`), network diagnostics (`termlink diagnostics`), validated config (`termlink config`), Developer SDK (`import { TermLink } from \"termlink\"`), tests, GitHub Actions CI/CD, full docs including VMware Scenarios A\342\200\223E, and `npm pack --dry-run` validation.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed & Written Files**:\n  - **Monorepo packages**:\n    - `/packages/core/package.json`, `/packages/core/src/index.ts` (types, config validator, filename sanitizer, path traversal guard, command risk detector, logger)\n    - `/packages/permissions/package.json`, `/packages/permissions/src/index.ts` (RBAC permission matrix & terminal access enforcement)\n    - `/packages/protocol/package.json`, `/packages/protocol/src/index.ts` (wire schemas, join target parser, signaling frame validator, peer-assisted distribution module)\n    - `/packages/identity/package.json`, `/packages/identity/src/index.ts` (Ed25519 + X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM, SHA-256 fingerprints, local `0o600` store & trust management)\n    - `/packages/room-engine/package.json`, `/packages/room-engine/src/index.ts` (2-digit codes, collision disambiguation, scrypt passwords, invites, sliding-window rate limiter, host approval, reconnect tokens)\n    - `/packages/file-transfer/package.json`, `/packages/file-transfer/src/index.ts` (streaming `StreamingFileSender` & `StreamingFileReceiver`, SHA-256 checks, `.part` staging, conflict-free naming)\n    - `/packages/terminal-session/package.json`, `/packages/terminal-session/src/index.ts` (cross-platform `resolvePlatformShell`, `SharedTerminalSession` with per-peer RBAC, locking, audit trail, and immediate shell termination fix)\n    - `/packages/networking/package.json`, `/packages/networking/src/index.ts` (`TopologyManager`, real RFC 5389 UDP `probeStunServer`, `DirectP2PTransport` with E2EE relay fallback)\n    - `/packages/diagnostics/package.json`, `/packages/diagnostics/src/index.ts` (`runDiagnostics`, `formatDiagnosticsText`, IP redaction unless `--detailed`)\n    - `/packages/sdk/package.json`, `/packages/sdk/src/index.ts` (`TermLink` client & `RoomSession` public Developer SDK)\n  - **Applications & Server**:\n    - `/apps/signaling-server/package.json`, `/apps/signaling-server/src/index.ts`, `/apps/signaling-server/src/standalone.ts`\n    - `/apps/cli/package.json`, `/apps/cli/src/config.ts`, `/apps/cli/src/ui.ts`, `/apps/cli/src/index.ts` (full CLI including `termlink`, `termlink 47`, `create`/`host`, `join`, `server`, `room`, `chat`, `send`, `receive`, `session share`, `diagnostics`, `config`, `devices`/`peers`, `trust`, `status`, `version`, `help`)\n    - `/server.ts` (pure headless Node `http` + `TermLinkSignalingServer` on port 3000 with `/ws`, `/health`, and plain-text `/join/:code` & `/invite/:token` instructions \342\200\224 no web UI)\n  - **Build, Packaging & Config**:\n    - `/scripts/build.mjs` (compiles via `esbuild` + `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` into `dist/bin/termlink.mjs`, `dist/signaling-server.mjs`, `dist/sdk/index.mjs`, and `dist/types/**/*.d.ts`)\n    - `/package.json` (`name: \"termlink\"`, `version: \"1.0.0\"`, `bin: { termlink, termlink-server }`, `main`, `types`, `exports`, `files: [\"dist\", \"README.md\", \"LICENSE\", \"SECURITY.md\"]`, scripts for `build`, `lint`, `test`, `cli`, `signaling`, `pack:check`)\n    - `/tsconfig.json`, `/tsconfig.build.json`, `/metadata.json`, `/.env.example`\n  - **Tests**:\n    - `/tests/unit/core-protocol.test.ts` (9 unit tests \342\200\224 previously passed 9/9)\n    - `/tests/security/security.test.ts` (3 security tests \342\200\224 previously passed 3/3)\n    - `/tests/integration/cli-processes.test.ts` (1 multi-process test spawning compiled `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs` and `node dist/signaling-server.mjs` \342\200\224 previously passed 1/1 in 3.7s)\n    - `/tests/integration/multi-peer.test.ts` (full 3-peer E2E test: create, 2-digit join + approval, 3-peer group, E2EE chat/PM, 160 KB SHA-256 file transfer, disconnect/reconnect, live shared terminal security \342\200\224 test assertions passed in 932ms, then hung on process exit due to interactive `bash -i` ignoring `SIGTERM`; fix was JUST applied to `/packages/terminal-session/src/index.ts` and has NOT yet been rebuilt or re-tested!)\n  - **Docs & CI/CD**:\n    - `/README.md`, `/SECURITY.md`, `/CONTRIBUTING.md`, `/LICENSE`, `/examples/sdk-basic.ts`\n    - `/docs/architecture.md`, `/docs/networking-and-vms.md`, `/docs/sdk-and-cli.md`, `/docs/troubleshooting.md`\n    - `/.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `/.github/workflows/release.yml`\n  - **Deleted Website Files**: `/src/` directory, `/index.html`, `/vite.config.ts`, and obsolete `/apps/cli/bin/termlink.mjs`.\n- **Installed Packages**: `ws`, `@types/ws`, `commander`, `chalk` (plus starter `esbuild`, `tsx`, `typescript`, etc.). Note: `react`, `react-dom`, `vite`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, `express` are still listed in `package.json` dependencies from the starter template (they are NOT bundled into `dist/` because `esbuild` uses `packages: \'external\'` and none of the CLI/SDK/server files import them).\n- **Skills Read**: `ultra-mode`, `frontend-design`, `computer-use`, `real-time-and-multi-user`.\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- Environment: Node `v22.23.2`, npm `10.9.8`, Linux x86_64 (`gvisor`).\n- Pure-JS/Node networking (`ws` + native `node:net` Direct TCP + `node:dgram` RFC 5389 STUN + native `node:crypto` Ed25519/X25519/AES-256-GCM) avoids brittle native C++ addon builds (`node-pty`, `wrtc`) across Windows/Linux/macOS/Node 22 while providing real direct P2P and E2EE relay fallback.\n- `esbuild` bundles `dist/bin/termlink.mjs` (159.8 kB), `dist/sdk/index.mjs` (78.7 kB), and `dist/signaling-server.mjs` (44.6 kB) cleanly into a 77.7 kB npm tarball (`termlink-1.0.0.tgz`, 17 files) verified with `npm pack --dry-run`.\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **User rejection of web frontend**: Built a React/Vite companion app in Turn 1; user explicitly requested ONLY the terminal npm package. Fixed by deleting `/src/`, `/index.html`, `/vite.config.ts`, replacing `server.ts` with a pure headless signaling server, and compiling real standalone Node CLI/SDK/server binaries in `dist/` via `scripts/build.mjs`.\n2. **`security.test.ts` race condition (`PEER_NOT_FOUND`)**: `roomHost.proposeCommand(\'TRUSTED-PEER\', ...)` fired before `room:updated` reached `roomHost`. Fixed in both `/packages/sdk/src/index.ts` (immediately appending member in `room:peer_joined`) and `/tests/security/security.test.ts` (awaiting `peerJoined` before calling `proposeCommand`). Verified passing (3/3).\n3. **15-second process hang after file transfer in `packages/sdk/src/index.ts`**: Un-cleared `setTimeout(..., 15_000)` inside `ackWaiters` and `setTimeout(resolve, 500)` in `disconnect()` kept Node\'s event loop alive. Fixed by calling `clearTimeout(timer)` on ACK/close and `.unref?.()` on safety timers.\n4. **Process hang after `multi-peer.test.ts` completed**: `SharedTerminalSession.stop()` sent `SIGTERM` to `bash -i`, which POSIX interactive bash ignores on Linux. Fixed in `/packages/terminal-session/src/index.ts` by closing `proc.stdin.end()` and sending `SIGKILL` on Unix. **Needs rebuild + re-test in next turn.**\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- No background tasks are currently running (all previous tasks completed or were cancelled).\n- Last edit made was to `/packages/terminal-session/src/index.ts` (`stop()` method). Therefore, `dist/` and test results are stale until rebuilt and re-run after this edit.\n- `package.json` still has starter web packages (`react`, `vite`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, etc.) in `dependencies` \342\200\224 optional quick cleanup if desired, OR leave untouched unless removing them cleanly via `replace_file_content` so `npm install -g termlink` doesn\'t pull unused React/Vite deps! Removing unused web deps from `package.json` `dependencies` (keeping `chalk`, `commander`, `ws`, `@types/ws`, `dotenv`) would make the published npm package much cleaner for `npm install -g termlink`! (Verify `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, and `npm test` afterwards.)\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **(Recommended cleanup)** Check `/package.json` and remove unused web/React/Vite/Tailwind dependencies (`@google/genai`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `@vitejs/plugin-react`, `express`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, `react`, `react-dom`, `vite`, and `@types/express`, `@types/react`, `@types/react-dom`, `autoprefixer`, `tailwindcss`) using `replace_file_content` so `npm install -g termlink` only installs actual CLI runtime dependencies (`chalk`, `commander`, `ws`, `dotenv`). Keep `esbuild`, `tsx`, `typescript`, `@types/node`, `@types/ws` in `devDependencies`.\n2. **Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`** to rebuild `dist/` (picking up the `SharedTerminalSession.stop()` fix) and verify zero TypeScript errors.\n3. **Run the complete test suite** after the rebuild and verify ALL tests pass AND exit cleanly without hanging:\n   - `./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test tests/unit/core-protocol.test.ts tests/security/security.test.ts tests/integration/multi-peer.test.ts tests/integration/cli-processes.test.ts`\n4. **Run `npm pack --dry-run` and smoke-test the compiled CLI** (`node dist/bin/termlink.mjs version` and `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs --help`) after the final build.\n5. **Provide a concise, honest summary** to the user confirming the web UI was completely removed, listing the pure npm terminal package structure, exact commands to run (`npm run build`, `npm run signaling` / `termlink server`, `npm run cli -- create`, `npm run cli -- 47`, `npm test`, `npm pack --dry-run`), verified test outcomes, and documented limitations (e.g., cross-OS Windows/macOS runs rely on GitHub Actions CI matrix since the container is Linux; `bash -i` uses piped stdio rather than native C++ `node-pty`).\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **No website / no React frontend**: User explicitly wants a pure terminal npm package (`termlink`). Do NOT recreate any web UI.\n- **No browser verification needed**: Because there is no web frontend, skip `playwright-cli` browser verification (pure CLI/backend package verified via unit, integration, security, and multi-process CLI tests + `npm pack --dry-run`).\n- **Verification rule**: Final build (`compile_applet` + `lint_applet` co-executed) and all tests must run **after** the last code edit. Never claim a test passed unless actually executed after the final edit.\n- **Honesty**: Clearly state what was verified locally on Linux vs. what requires Windows/macOS/VMware hardware or GitHub Actions matrix. Do not publish to npm automatically.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 159
