  planner_response {
    response: "Removed the web frontend completely (`/src`, `index.html`, `vite.config.ts`, and all React/Vite/Tailwind/Express dependencies) and converted the project into a pure, standalone **Node.js npm CLI package (`termlink`)** that runs directly in the computer\'s terminal.\n\n### What Is Included\n- **Installable npm Package (`termlink@1.0.0`)**:\n  - Binaries: `termlink` (interactive terminal CLI) and `termlink-server` (self-hosted signaling server)\n  - Public Developer SDK: `import { TermLink } from \"termlink\"` with generated TypeScript `.d.ts` definitions\n  - Runtime dependencies trimmed to only `chalk`, `commander`, `dotenv`, and `ws`\n- **Terminal Collaboration Features**:\n  - **2-Digit Quick-Connect (`00`\342\200\223`99`) & Secure Invites**: Collision handling, TTL expiry, sliding-window rate limiting, scrypt room passwords, one-time/expiring/role-scoped invite tokens, and host join approval enabled by default.\n  - **Real P2P Networking & E2EE**: Ed25519 + X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM end-to-end encryption, Direct TCP peer links with RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing, and opaque E2EE relay fallback with honest transport status reporting (`Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, `Disconnected`). Supports 2\342\200\2238 peer full mesh and 9\342\200\22320 peer hybrid topology.\n  - **Terminal Chat & Safe Command Proposals**: Group chat, private `/msg` messages, slash commands (`/members`, `/status`, `/clear`, `/help`, `/leave`), and dangerous-command risk detection (proposals never auto-execute).\n  - **Streaming P2P File Transfer**: 64 KiB chunked streaming with per-chunk and full-file SHA-256 integrity checks, pause/resume/cancel, recipient approval prompts, filename sanitization, path traversal/symlink guards, conflict-free file naming, and a peer-assisted distribution protocol module.\n  - **Opt-in Shared Terminal Sessions**: Disabled by default, cross-platform shell detection (`PowerShell` on Windows, `bash`/`zsh`/`sh` on Linux/macOS), per-peer `read-only` / `interactive` / `disabled` RBAC, session lock, instant revocation, and audit logging.\n  - **Identity, Config & Diagnostics**: Local `0o600` key & trust store (`termlink devices`, `termlink trust`), validated config (`termlink config`), and real network/STUN/signaling diagnostics (`termlink diagnostics`).\n- **Docs & CI/CD**: Full documentation covering architecture, VMware/VirtualBox/WSL2 networking scenarios (A\342\200\223E), CLI/SDK usage, troubleshooting, security policy, and GitHub Actions workflows for Linux, macOS, and Windows.\n\n### How to Run Locally in Your Terminal\n```bash\n# 1. Build the CLI, signaling server, and SDK bundles\nnpm run build\n\n# 2. Start the signaling server (or run `termlink server` after `npm link`)\nnpm run signaling\n\n# 3. Host a room in terminal #1\nnpm run cli -- create --server ws://127.0.0.1:3000/ws --name Alice\n\n# 4. Join using the 2-digit code (e.g. 47) in terminal #2\nnpm run cli -- 47 --server ws://127.0.0.1:3000/ws --name Bob\n\n# Or install globally from this repo to run `termlink` directly anywhere:\nnpm link\ntermlink --help\ntermlink create\ntermlink 47\ntermlink diagnostics\n```\n\n### Verification & Notes\n- **Build & Type-check**: `npm run build` and `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- **Automated Tests**: All **14/14 tests passed** cleanly (`npm test`), including unit tests, security tests (rate limiting, expired/revoked/one-time invites, host rejection, non-auto-executing command proposals), a 3-peer E2E lifecycle test (create, 2-digit join + approval, E2EE chat, 160 KiB SHA-256 file transfer, disconnect/reconnect, live shared terminal security), and a multi-process test spawning the compiled `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs` and `node dist/signaling-server.mjs` binaries.\n- **Package Check**: `npm pack --dry-run` verified `termlink-1.0.0.tgz` (77.8 kB compressed, 17 files, zero web assets).\n- **Environment Limitations**: Local tests ran on Linux x86_64 (Node 22); Windows/macOS and VMware NAT/bridged topologies are covered via cross-platform shell/network code and the multi-OS GitHub Actions CI matrix rather than executed on physical Windows/macOS/VMware hardware here. Shared terminal sessions use standard piped child-process stdio rather than native C++ `node-pty` to keep cross-platform `npm install` free of native compiler build failures."
    message_id: "tgMAa87BK6Cfz7IPvNunwA4"
    modified_response: "Removed the web frontend completely (`/src`, `index.html`, `vite.config.ts`, and all React/Vite/Tailwind/Express dependencies) and converted the project into a pure, standalone **Node.js npm CLI package (`termlink`)** that runs directly in the computer\'s terminal.\n\n### What Is Included\n- **Installable npm Package (`termlink@1.0.0`)**:\n  - Binaries: `termlink` (interactive terminal CLI) and `termlink-server` (self-hosted signaling server)\n  - Public Developer SDK: `import { TermLink } from \"termlink\"` with generated TypeScript `.d.ts` definitions\n  - Runtime dependencies trimmed to only `chalk`, `commander`, `dotenv`, and `ws`\n- **Terminal Collaboration Features**:\n  - **2-Digit Quick-Connect (`00`\342\200\223`99`) & Secure Invites**: Collision handling, TTL expiry, sliding-window rate limiting, scrypt room passwords, one-time/expiring/role-scoped invite tokens, and host join approval enabled by default.\n  - **Real P2P Networking & E2EE**: Ed25519 + X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM end-to-end encryption, Direct TCP peer links with RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing, and opaque E2EE relay fallback with honest transport status reporting (`Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, `Disconnected`). Supports 2\342\200\2238 peer full mesh and 9\342\200\22320 peer hybrid topology.\n  - **Terminal Chat & Safe Command Proposals**: Group chat, private `/msg` messages, slash commands (`/members`, `/status`, `/clear`, `/help`, `/leave`), and dangerous-command risk detection (proposals never auto-execute).\n  - **Streaming P2P File Transfer**: 64 KiB chunked streaming with per-chunk and full-file SHA-256 integrity checks, pause/resume/cancel, recipient approval prompts, filename sanitization, path traversal/symlink guards, conflict-free file naming, and a peer-assisted distribution protocol module.\n  - **Opt-in Shared Terminal Sessions**: Disabled by default, cross-platform shell detection (`PowerShell` on Windows, `bash`/`zsh`/`sh` on Linux/macOS), per-peer `read-only` / `interactive` / `disabled` RBAC, session lock, instant revocation, and audit logging.\n  - **Identity, Config & Diagnostics**: Local `0o600` key & trust store (`termlink devices`, `termlink trust`), validated config (`termlink config`), and real network/STUN/signaling diagnostics (`termlink diagnostics`).\n- **Docs & CI/CD**: Full documentation covering architecture, VMware/VirtualBox/WSL2 networking scenarios (A\342\200\223E), CLI/SDK usage, troubleshooting, security policy, and GitHub Actions workflows for Linux, macOS, and Windows.\n\n### How to Run Locally in Your Terminal\n```bash\n# 1. Build the CLI, signaling server, and SDK bundles\nnpm run build\n\n# 2. Start the signaling server (or run `termlink server` after `npm link`)\nnpm run signaling\n\n# 3. Host a room in terminal #1\nnpm run cli -- create --server ws://127.0.0.1:3000/ws --name Alice\n\n# 4. Join using the 2-digit code (e.g. 47) in terminal #2\nnpm run cli -- 47 --server ws://127.0.0.1:3000/ws --name Bob\n\n# Or install globally from this repo to run `termlink` directly anywhere:\nnpm link\ntermlink --help\ntermlink create\ntermlink 47\ntermlink diagnostics\n```\n\n### Verification & Notes\n- **Build & Type-check**: `npm run build` and `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- **Automated Tests**: All **14/14 tests passed** cleanly (`npm test`), including unit tests, security tests (rate limiting, expired/revoked/one-time invites, host rejection, non-auto-executing command proposals), a 3-peer E2E lifecycle test (create, 2-digit join + approval, E2EE chat, 160 KiB SHA-256 file transfer, disconnect/reconnect, live shared terminal security), and a multi-process test spawning the compiled `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs` and `node dist/signaling-server.mjs` binaries.\n- **Package Check**: `npm pack --dry-run` verified `termlink-1.0.0.tgz` (77.8 kB compressed, 17 files, zero web assets).\n- **Environment Limitations**: Local tests ran on Linux x86_64 (Node 22); Windows/macOS and VMware NAT/bridged topologies are covered via cross-platform shell/network code and the multi-OS GitHub Actions CI matrix rather than executed on physical Windows/macOS/VMware hardware here. Shared terminal sessions use standard piped child-process stdio rather than native C++ `node-pty` to keep cross-platform `npm install` free of native compiler build failures."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\206\004\n\203\004\001i\024}\023\214nj\253\207\a1 @M\004\276\331#\257\\\304\353\372\213}T\213\205\240\177\266\302u\277`]\251\037\271^)\253\323\336\002o\246\315\340\003\266\371\240\305\307\275PGr\177\334 \341^\354\343{}\365G\332\'\223/\310\372\021\322;}\263%\233\244\t\320\036\":\231\364\245\242\004\332\b\215nFS\004J\315\246\204UU\346\220:g\371m\333\006\322l\265(\233>\210\313\336\247\363\342\000\365h\177\362\314!\222\356N\227\231\261\3742p\005\022\'#\372\202\201\377\377\332\301\203\347\353\346v\207T:\\\t5\371\021\312\344eq\024\036\306\337\303\v\217\341\200\225\031\336\310\26281)i~\203\240_AF\311\215\277G-\217\212x\006\377rT\321\0373\370\370D\223R2\031M\352\330\250\344\220\234\241H+~\230MY8A\033\036\361\025i.\326\307\225~f\373|\270[\276<\207\001\320\363Y:<\243Y\025n\3608e\a;\000,\277J\306\244y\241\177\321\255\371\225\n\235\222\356\376\242T\2423\202\r\207kY\363I\306\256\350AL\374\377K\016\240w\234\273T\nG\375w\005\236\255z\334<\214\234\354\2435M7x\217\363\332~t\314\230\264\250v\231\353wt%\255\367\371$\276I\364]\332\030\034q\224GE\023\304\034\006P/}\270\257\366Y\245\001\345\261\025\224\362\312\2150&\260\a\340\351 >v\313\312\320\2646\026\346\206r:\235|9\234=&\276\372\372,\364Z\037P\204\267\261\006?\274;\366\263\323>\327\320\226\'3 J\000\323\225\265D\257a\356\313\215\306\237\322\235\351}\246-\351\344\213\276\024\v\265\b\233\n\356\315\200\347\350\242)\207\255\273k\272C\v\221jC\246K\026\305\367*\006\346\277PaV(5?\247\254A\222g\004g=\335\212\236\263\214n<f\002U\310&\233`PSc\347"
