  planner_response {
    response: "The web UI (`React`, `Vite`, `index.html`, `src/`, and all unused web dependencies) has been completely removed. The project is now a pure Node.js terminal **npm package** (`termlink`) with standalone CLI binaries, a self-hostable signaling server, and a TypeScript/ESM Developer SDK.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **CLI Executables (`bin` in `package.json`)**:\n  - `termlink` \342\200\224 interactive terminal CLI (`termlink`, `termlink 47`, `create`/`host`, `join`, `server`, `room`, `chat`, `send`, `receive`, `session share`, `diagnostics`, `config`, `devices`/`peers`, `trust`, `status`, `version`, `help`)\n  - `termlink-server` \342\200\224 standalone headless WebSocket signaling server (no web UI; plain-text `/join/:code` and `/invite/:token` instructions + `/health` JSON)\n- **Core Capabilities**:\n  - **2-Digit Quick-Connect Codes (`00`\342\200\223`99`) & Invites**: Collision handling, TTL expiration, scrypt room passwords, sliding-window rate limiting, one-time/role-scoped revocable invitation tokens, and host approval by default.\n  - **Real P2P Networking & E2EE**: Direct TCP peer transport with X25519 key agreement, Ed25519 authentication, HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM encryption, RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing, full mesh (2\342\200\2238 peers) / hybrid topology (9\342\200\22320 peers), and opaque E2EE relay fallback with accurate transport reporting (`Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, `Disconnected`).\n  - **Streaming P2P File Transfer**: 64 KiB chunked streaming, per-chunk and full-file SHA-256 verification, backpressure, explicit recipient approval, path traversal / symlink guards, and conflict-free file naming.\n  - **Opt-In Shared Terminal & Command Proposals**: Disabled by default, cross-platform shell selection (PowerShell on Windows, `$SHELL`/`bash`/`zsh`/`sh` on Linux/macOS), per-peer `read-only` / `interactive` / `disabled` RBAC, session locking, instant revocation, audit log, and non-auto-executing command risk detection.\n  - **Developer SDK & Docs**: `import { TermLink } from \"termlink\"` with generated `.d.ts` types, GitHub Actions CI/release workflows, and VMware / NAT / troubleshooting documentation (`docs/`).\n\n### How to Run & Install Locally\n```bash\n# 1. Build the CLI, signaling server, SDK, and type definitions\nnpm run build\n\n# 2. Start a local signaling server (Terminal 1)\nnpm run signaling\n\n# 3. Host a room (Terminal 2)\nnpm run cli -- create\n\n# 4. Join by 2-digit code or invite link (Terminal 3)\nnpm run cli -- 47\n\n# Optional: install globally from this repo\nnpm install -g .\ntermlink --help\n```\n\n### Verification Results\n- **Build & Type-Check**: `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` both succeeded with zero errors.\n- **Automated Tests (`14/14` passing)**:\n  - 9 unit tests (2-digit codes, target parser, E2EE & tamper detection, RBAC, collision resolution, path traversal/conflict-free naming, command risk checks, topology, signaling validation)\n  - 3 security tests (rate limiting, expired/revoked/reused invites, live unauthorized rejection & non-executing command proposals)\n  - 1 full 3-peer end-to-end integration test (create, join + approval, group E2EE chat/PM, 160 KB SHA-256 file transfer, disconnect/reconnect, shared terminal permission enforcement)\n  - 1 compiled multi-process CLI binary integration test spawning `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs` and `node dist/signaling-server.mjs`\n- **Packaging**: `npm pack --dry-run` produced `termlink-1.0.0.tgz` (17 files, 77.8 kB packed) containing only runtime CLI/server/SDK artifacts (`chalk`, `commander`, `dotenv`, `ws`).\n\n### Current Limitations\n- Tests were verified in this Linux (`x86_64`) environment; native Windows/macOS and physical VMware NAT/Bridged/Host-Only setups should be verified on target hosts or via the included GitHub Actions matrix workflow.\n- Shared terminal sessions use cross-platform piped stdio rather than native C++ `node-pty` addons so `npm install -g termlink` stays zero-native-build across Node 20+."
    message_id: "1QMAa4WDHr6hz7IPuYLCkQg"
    modified_response: "The web UI (`React`, `Vite`, `index.html`, `src/`, and all unused web dependencies) has been completely removed. The project is now a pure Node.js terminal **npm package** (`termlink`) with standalone CLI binaries, a self-hostable signaling server, and a TypeScript/ESM Developer SDK.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **CLI Executables (`bin` in `package.json`)**:\n  - `termlink` \342\200\224 interactive terminal CLI (`termlink`, `termlink 47`, `create`/`host`, `join`, `server`, `room`, `chat`, `send`, `receive`, `session share`, `diagnostics`, `config`, `devices`/`peers`, `trust`, `status`, `version`, `help`)\n  - `termlink-server` \342\200\224 standalone headless WebSocket signaling server (no web UI; plain-text `/join/:code` and `/invite/:token` instructions + `/health` JSON)\n- **Core Capabilities**:\n  - **2-Digit Quick-Connect Codes (`00`\342\200\223`99`) & Invites**: Collision handling, TTL expiration, scrypt room passwords, sliding-window rate limiting, one-time/role-scoped revocable invitation tokens, and host approval by default.\n  - **Real P2P Networking & E2EE**: Direct TCP peer transport with X25519 key agreement, Ed25519 authentication, HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM encryption, RFC 5389 UDP STUN probing, full mesh (2\342\200\2238 peers) / hybrid topology (9\342\200\22320 peers), and opaque E2EE relay fallback with accurate transport reporting (`Direct P2P`, `Local network`, `VPN`, `Relayed`, `Connecting`, `Disconnected`).\n  - **Streaming P2P File Transfer**: 64 KiB chunked streaming, per-chunk and full-file SHA-256 verification, backpressure, explicit recipient approval, path traversal / symlink guards, and conflict-free file naming.\n  - **Opt-In Shared Terminal & Command Proposals**: Disabled by default, cross-platform shell selection (PowerShell on Windows, `$SHELL`/`bash`/`zsh`/`sh` on Linux/macOS), per-peer `read-only` / `interactive` / `disabled` RBAC, session locking, instant revocation, audit log, and non-auto-executing command risk detection.\n  - **Developer SDK & Docs**: `import { TermLink } from \"termlink\"` with generated `.d.ts` types, GitHub Actions CI/release workflows, and VMware / NAT / troubleshooting documentation (`docs/`).\n\n### How to Run & Install Locally\n```bash\n# 1. Build the CLI, signaling server, SDK, and type definitions\nnpm run build\n\n# 2. Start a local signaling server (Terminal 1)\nnpm run signaling\n\n# 3. Host a room (Terminal 2)\nnpm run cli -- create\n\n# 4. Join by 2-digit code or invite link (Terminal 3)\nnpm run cli -- 47\n\n# Optional: install globally from this repo\nnpm install -g .\ntermlink --help\n```\n\n### Verification Results\n- **Build & Type-Check**: `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` both succeeded with zero errors.\n- **Automated Tests (`14/14` passing)**:\n  - 9 unit tests (2-digit codes, target parser, E2EE & tamper detection, RBAC, collision resolution, path traversal/conflict-free naming, command risk checks, topology, signaling validation)\n  - 3 security tests (rate limiting, expired/revoked/reused invites, live unauthorized rejection & non-executing command proposals)\n  - 1 full 3-peer end-to-end integration test (create, join + approval, group E2EE chat/PM, 160 KB SHA-256 file transfer, disconnect/reconnect, shared terminal permission enforcement)\n  - 1 compiled multi-process CLI binary integration test spawning `node dist/bin/termlink.mjs` and `node dist/signaling-server.mjs`\n- **Packaging**: `npm pack --dry-run` produced `termlink-1.0.0.tgz` (17 files, 77.8 kB packed) containing only runtime CLI/server/SDK artifacts (`chalk`, `commander`, `dotenv`, `ws`).\n\n### Current Limitations\n- Tests were verified in this Linux (`x86_64`) environment; native Windows/macOS and physical VMware NAT/Bridged/Host-Only setups should be verified on target hosts or via the included GitHub Actions matrix workflow.\n- Shared terminal sessions use cross-platform piped stdio rather than native C++ `node-pty` addons so `npm install -g termlink` stays zero-native-build across Node 20+."
